      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:52927/libvirt-10-4-slackware-current-iptables/images/libvirt.png&#34; &gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#xA;    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;&#xA;    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;    decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;    fetchpriority=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;    alt=&#34;&#34;&#xA;    width=&#34;300&#34;&#xA;    height=&#34;238&#34;&#xA;    src=&#34;http://localhost:52927/libvirt-10-4-slackware-current-iptables/images/libvirt-300x238.png&#34;&#xA;    srcset=&#34;http://localhost:52927/libvirt-10-4-slackware-current-iptables/images/libvirt-300x238.png 800w, http://localhost:52927/libvirt-10-4-slackware-current-iptables/images/libvirt-300x238.png 1280w&#34;&#xA;    sizes=&#34;(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 65vw&#34;&#xA;    data-zoom-src=&#34;http://localhost:52927/libvirt-10-4-slackware-current-iptables/images/libvirt-300x238.png&#34;&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Salve pessoal!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tive um problema interessante após a última atualização dos softwares que utilizo no meu &lt;strong&gt;Slackware&lt;/strong&gt;. Um desses softwares é o libvirt, que utilizo para usar o &lt;strong&gt;KVM&lt;/strong&gt; como solução de virtualização.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
